{
  "name": "vector_light_shadow_wall",
  "saveFile": "minimal_colony.rws",
  "description": "Issue #166: a lamp shadow stops at the wall instead of crossing it. Two lit rooms separated by a one-cell wall, a colonist standing against that wall, and the lamp lighting them six cells away on the far side — so the shadow runs at the wall and, unclipped, out the other side. THE SECOND LAMP IS LOAD-BEARING, not scenery: an escaped shadow lands on the neighbouring room's floor, and a black quad on UNLIT ground is invisible however wrong it is, so without a lamp over there the bug photographs as nothing. The reach probe is the assertion — unclipped it reads the full geometric length, clipped it reads the distance from the caster to the wall — because the difference on screen is a sliver of overhang past a wall and a median over the frame cannot see it. Peak and rosette are pinned across both arms to show the clip changes how FAR a shadow goes and not how dark it is.",
